    <node id="&quot;WHO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The WHO is an international organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for health policies, including those related to physical activity and chronic diseases."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international health organization that addresses major public health concerns."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization responsible for global health policies and programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international public health organization that conducts research on nutrition-related topics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"WHO is an international organization providing guidelines on breastfeeding and nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"WHO refers to the World Health Organization, an international organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization responsible for global health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization responsible for global health policies and services."&lt;SEP&gt;"WHO (World Health Organization) is an international organization that sets global health policies and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"WHO is an international organization responsible for global health policies and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization that aims to improve global health outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization that has developed guidelines for healthcare, including those related to tobacco control."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization that promotes global health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international organization that provides guidance on global health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"WHO (World Health Organization) is a global health authority that sets standards and recommendations for various health-related issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"World Health Organization, mentioned as a reference for scientific evidence"&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international agency that publishes various reports and guidelines on cancer control, early detection, and screening."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization responsible for global health policies and programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is mentioned as a global entity providing health guidelines and recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"WHO is a global health organization that provides recommendations for breast cancer screening."</data>
