    <node id="&quot;FAMÍLIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">**Família**

The Família refers to the family unit, which plays a crucial role in promoting health, preventing chronic diseases, and supporting children's social and psychological development. This organization consists of related individuals by blood, marriage, or adoption, and its members may be influenced by various factors such as education, ideas about importance of education in preventing violence, and access to healthcare services.

The Família is a social group that can contribute to or trigger depression, but also provides resources and support to its members. It plays an important role in evaluating and addressing sleep problems in children, providing care and support to patients, and promoting health and safety measures among its members.

Moreover, the Família is involved in child health and development, including preventing accidents, supporting mental health attention for children and adolescents, and providing care and support to those with chronic conditions. Family influence extends to adolescents' choices, consumption of food, and physical activity, while family support and involvement are essential for patient adherence to treatment.

The Família can provide a sense of belonging and identity for its members, but it may also be influenced by external factors such as social forces of consumption and drug trafficking. The organization can benefit from Palliative Care and support during times of crisis, particularly when dealing with complex conditions like obesity or chronic illnesses.

Overall, the Família is an essential entity that plays a crucial role in promoting health, preventing disease, and supporting well-being among its members, especially children and adolescents.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6463366509c64fa7fb65802a7a2f177f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c7c4d19c5987039ebca6c0ab688024e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3e17cf08a9ae0761a384304f2fd27c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad2cdeef537ddce2a15448e3e445fe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6716d83f29bc8110d51945c30631f78e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-981422ef7d9d7de8dfc81ebc47669920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de199e955ca0907ebfe66e72edf13a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e55e309cf9a66e4387eeff8a0af7488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a0d01490bf5a6ab0cff6882f8beb9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182b697ad2228ca2d498d567d6be30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215970c8788330467e055b822a5be40e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8617fcc0448a6129ef38ea96306f2b8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19228cb7985c55d5bcdefcec56bb535d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b5e275006cd71a7686e3fb3c19ad7de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6513b490911790fb232edf96d75813e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b1c79f561d6423f4cc0a19d431ccf95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea906d795bda0cd96c1786b0da7ff4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fafb8b2529819deb56ac5f391b3309b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c532157f4a308e14e573d17246a0c92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d80b36b2088fd3430ac9d2913d3d01d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb9ea51ef9fe3474e11a9e9f37128fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a51102865c369564d8aa119329c7d05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48bf3ee1c14080b44158c5b782ac1c69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b14f7a93d37b8c17c5bed60ccac0b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f1c13b78f82267ffcb2d002acf95560&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2e8268c1155db3eb90790ad79e9567&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdcedeee4b447e168accae1f8cc0bbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44d670f4de331793174bd26e9d438e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-483efc8a7d3c5dc5d248da4b6a44e81e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85f44bd4bd82e81b4bff04ea604a0615&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288f6abb61666f94c6198793c72cba7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d5f7ecfead2d4b99b3193e76214fb7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c363e6cb6655d7d1fc224f961ad27950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876162e541368a7f03b67b85639e5d6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f90ad9506dc1f3f363b250c308cf8f42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f74057a3d2a1ff5abeb79cdfb51a3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-400ce3dac690019f4a75de65ee8987a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8329b5264a11203795c34d3c6a9c942</data>
