    <node id="&quot;MINISTÉRIO DA SAÚDE | SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE | DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ministério da Saúde is the Brazilian Ministry of Health, responsible for various departments including Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde and Departamento de Atenção Básica."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ministério da Saúde | Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde | Departamento de Atenção Básica is the Ministry of Health, with its Secretariat and Department for Basic Care."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ministry of Health, Department of Attention to Health, and Department of Basic Attention are government organizations responsible for healthcare in Brazil."&lt;SEP&gt;Here is the comprehensive summary of the data provided:

**MINISTÉRIO DA SAÚDE | SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE | DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA**

The MINISTÉRIO DA SAÚDE (Ministry of Health) and its departments, including the SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE (Secretary of Attention to Health) and DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA (Department of Basic Care), are government agencies responsible for healthcare in Brazil. They provide a range of services, including basic health care, disease prevention, and health policies.

The Department of Basic Care is specifically responsible for providing primary care services to the population, as well as healthcare programs and policies. The Secretary of Attention to Health plays a key role in women's health policies, and the Ministry of Health promotes healthy eating habits and provides guidelines for managing diseases, particularly focusing on cancer detection and treatment (including breast cancer).

The Department of Basic Care is responsible for providing basic health care services to the population, while the Secretary of Attention to Health focuses on women's health policies. The Ministry of Health as a whole provides information and recommendations on health topics.

Overall, the MINISTÉRIO DA SAÚDE | SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE | DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA are key government agencies in Brazil responsible for promoting healthy eating habits, disease prevention, and providing basic health care services to the population.</data>
