    <node id="&quot;DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Departamento de Atenção Básica is a department within the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde, responsible for basic attention in healthcare."&lt;SEP&gt;Here is a comprehensive summary of the data provided:

**Departamento de Atenção Básica (DBA)**

The Departamento de Atenção Básica (DBA), also known as the Department of Basic Attention or Department of Basic Care, is a department within the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde and the Brazilian Ministry of Health in Brazil. It is responsible for providing basic healthcare services to the public, focusing on primary healthcare and community-based services.

The DBA's responsibilities include:

* Providing basic healthcare services to the public
* Implementing health policies and programs at the local level
* Promoting healthy eating habits and protecting public health
* Handling basic healthcare matters
* Focusing on primary healthcare and community-based services

Specifically, the department provides primary care services, including basic health care and attention to health, as well as strategies for obesity prevention and managing hypertension. It is also responsible for implementing health policies and programs at the local level, promoting healthy eating habits, and providing basic healthcare services.

The DBA's work includes:

* Providing nutrition advice
* Promoting breastfeeding
* Implementing the NutriSUS strategy to ensure the health of Brazilian children
* Providing information on proper hand washing and utensil cleaning when preparing infant formula
* Focusing on primary care services in Brazil

Overall, the Departamento de Atenção Básica (DBA) is a vital component of Brazil's Ministry of Health, dedicated to providing essential healthcare services to its citizens.</data>
