    <node id="&quot;HIPERGLICEMIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hiperglicemia refers to abnormally high levels of glucose in the blood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hiperglicemia refers to high blood sugar levels, which are a hallmark of diabetes mellitus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hyperglycemia is a concept referring to the condition of having high blood sugar levels, which can be caused by various factors including Type 1 and Type 2 Diabetes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hyperglycemia is a condition where blood glucose levels are too high."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hyperglycemia is an elevated blood sugar level, which can lead to various complications if not managed properly."&lt;SEP&gt;"hiperglicemia is a condition characterized by high blood sugar levels, which can lead to complications in people with diabetes."</data>
