      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Organização Mundial da Saúde é uma organização internacional que trabalha para melhorar a saúde global."&lt;SEP&gt;"Author of Child and adolescent mental policies and plans"&lt;SEP&gt;"International organization responsible for global health"&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) provides guidelines for managing Hypertensive Arterial Systemic (HAS) disease."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization responsible for global public health policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization that promotes health and well-being, including diabetes management."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization that provides guidelines for managing diabetes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization published a report in 2003 regarding the economic impact of diabetes worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION is an international health organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"World Health Organization is an international organization that sets health standards and guidelines globally."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization that provides guidelines for national cancer control programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"International public health authority coordinating responses to global health issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION is an international organization that provides guidance on public health issues, including those related to tobacco addiction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is a global agency responsible for promoting and protecting health worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for international public health, which includes addressing the global issue of tobacco use."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international agency that promotes global health policies and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is an international organization responsible for global health policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION is an organization that provides information on the health risks and consequences of smoking."&lt;SEP&gt;"The WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION is an international agency responsible for health and nutrition policies worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization (WHO) is an international public health agency that publishes guidelines on breastfeeding, infant feeding, and nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization recommends that the introduction of solid foods should be done at six months of age for infants fed with formula."&lt;SEP&gt;"The World Health Organization is a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for international public health."</data>
