    <node id="&quot;HAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HAS is a condition where blood pressure is above 140/90mmHg, indicating hypertension."&lt;SEP&gt;"HAS is the entity representing Hypertension Arterial Sistêmica."&lt;SEP&gt;"HAS stands for High Arterial System, referring to high blood pressure or hypertension."&lt;SEP&gt;"HAS stands for High Blood Pressure, a measurement of systolic and diastolic pressure that indicates the severity of hypertension."&lt;SEP&gt;"HAS stands for Hypertension Arterial Sistêmica, an event or condition related to high blood pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hypertensive Arterial Systemic (HAS) disease is a condition characterized by high blood pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"HAS stands for Hypertensive Arterial System, an organization that emphasizes the importance of quitting smoking in controlling high blood pressure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hypertensive Arterial Systemic"&lt;SEP&gt;"HAS stands for Hipertensão Arterial, a medical condition with symptoms and treatment."</data>
