    <node id="&quot;CÂNCER DO COLO DO ÚTERO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of cancer that affects women."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical Cancer is an event that can affect women."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical Cancer"&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer is a type of cancer affecting the cervix, which can be diagnosed through colposcopy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer is a type of cancer affecting the cervix, which can be prevented through vaccination and early detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer is a type of cancer affecting the female population, with high incidence rates worldwide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer is a type of cancer that affects the cervix in women."&lt;SEP&gt;"Câncer do Colo do Útero is a medical condition that affects the cervix, mentioned in the context of cancer control measures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Câncer do Colo do Útero is a type of cancer that affects the cervix."&lt;SEP&gt;"Câncer do colo do útero is a type of cancer that affects the cervix in women."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer is a type of cancer that affects the cervix in women."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cervical cancer is an event that can be prevented and treated through early detection."</data>
