      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Falls are an event where an individual loses balance and lands on the ground, often resulting in injuries or health issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSTITUCIONALIZAÇÃO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Institutionalization refers to the process of placing an individual in a care facility or nursing home due to health issues or decline in functional capacity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEDAS &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Falls are an event where an individual loses balance and lands on the ground, often resulting in injuries or health issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IDOSOS COM MAIS DE 80 ANOS &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Older adults over 80 years old are a group of individuals who experience significant physical decline and potential health issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEXO FEMININO &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Female sex is a demographic characteristic that can increase the risk of falls among older adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMOBILIDADE &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immobility refers to a condition where an individual has limited or no mobility, increasing the risk of falls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEDAS PRECEDENTES &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Previous falls are a history of experiencing falls, which can increase the likelihood of future falls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EQUILÍBRIO DIMINUÍDO &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reduced balance refers to a condition where an individual has difficulty maintaining their equilibrium, increasing the risk of falls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARCHA LENTA E COM PASSOS CURTOS &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Slow and short steps refer to a gait pattern that can increase the risk of falls among older adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAIXA APTIDÃO FÍSICA &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low physical ability refers to a condition where an individual has limited strength, flexibility, or endurance, increasing the risk of falls."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRAQUEZA MUSCULAR DE MMII E MMSS (HAND GRIP) &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muscular weakness in hand grip is a measure of muscle strength that can indicate increased risk of falls among older adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALTERAÇÕES COGNITIVAS &quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cognitive changes refer to a decline in mental function, which can increase the risk of falls among older adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ede7f75e574b6d3b75bdcc194096b396</data>
    </node>
