      <data key="d1">"Parkinson's disease is a neurological condition affecting movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e214a761cbb1193242c87168fe80c31b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIDROCEFALIA NORMOTENSA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Normal pressure hydrocephalus is a condition where fluid accumulates in the brain, leading to increased intracranial pressure."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e214a761cbb1193242c87168fe80c31b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRÓSTATA AUMENTADA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An enlarged prostate gland can cause urination difficulties."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e214a761cbb1193242c87168fe80c31b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXCESSO DE DÉBITO URINÁRIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyuria is a condition characterized by excessive urine production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e214a761cbb1193242c87168fe80c31b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OBSTIPAÇÃO INTESTINAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Constipation can lead to urinary incontinence due to fecaloma impactation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e214a761cbb1193242c87168fe80c31b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FECALOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecaloma refers to the accumulation of feces that can cause urinary and fecal incontinence."</data>
