    <node id="&quot;DEMÊNCIA VASCULAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Demência Vascular is a type of dementia characterized by abrupt onset, usually after a vascular episode."&lt;SEP&gt;"Vascular dementia is not a disease but a heterogeneous group of syndromes resulting from various vascular mechanisms and cerebral changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30cba53594387889bd0cde4b9ae4bf18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOENÇA DE ALZHEIMER (DA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doença de Alzheimer (DA) is a multifactorial disease that affects cognitive function and causes demência."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30cba53594387889bd0cde4b9ae4bf18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIPOS DE DEMÊNCIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tipos de Demência is an event that categorizes various types of dementias."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30cba53594387889bd0cde4b9ae4bf18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEMÊNCIAS FRONTOTEMPORAIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Demências Frontotemporais refers to a group of dementia disorders affecting frontal and temporal lobes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30cba53594387889bd0cde4b9ae4bf18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DOENÇA DE PICK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Doença de Pick is a type of demência characterized by early onset, personality changes, and language alterations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-30cba53594387889bd0cde4b9ae4bf18</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DA EVOLUI EM TRÊS ESTÁGIOS HIERÁRQUICOS...&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DA refers to a process that evolves through three stages, which can undergo changes..."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FASE INICIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Initial phase is characterized by vague and diffuse symptoms that develop insidiously, with memory compromise as the most prominent and early symptom."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SÍNDROME DO ENTARDECER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Twilight syndrome refers to confusion mental and behavioral alterations, often occurring near sunset time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FASE INTERMEDIÁRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intermediate phase is characterized by more pronounced deterioration of memory deficits and the involvement of other cognitive domains, such as aphasia, agnosia, visual-spatial and visual-constructive impairments, and apraxia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FASE AVANÇADA OU ESTÁGIO TERMINAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Advanced or terminal stage refers to severe compromise of all cognitive functions, with difficulty in recognizing people and familiar spaces, total dependency on others for activities of daily living, significant reduction in language fluency, and eventual mutism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AVD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AVD refers to another stage of cognitive decline, marked by further deterioration of daily activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SÍNDROME DA IMOBILIDADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Syndrome of immobility refers to a condition where individuals are severely compromised cognitively and become bedridden."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LESÕES TROMBOEMBÓLICAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thromboembolic lesions refer to large blood clots that cause damage to the brain."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AFASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aphasia refers to a condition where individuals experience difficulty with language, including naming objects and understanding spoken words."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGNOSIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agnosia refers to a condition where individuals have difficulty recognizing objects, people, sounds, or shapes despite maintaining intact sensory function."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APRAXIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apraxia refers to a neurological disorder characterized by difficulty executing precise movements and gestures that require patterns of memory or sequential movement."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARAFASIAS VERBAIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Verbal paraplasia refers to the use of one word in place of another, often without any evident understanding of the replaced word."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERSEVERAÇÕES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Perseverations refer to the repetition of ideas or representations, often without any new information being added."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTOCOLO CLÍNICO E DIRETRIZES TERAPÊUTICAS – DEMÊNCIA POR DOENÇA DE ALZHEIMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
