    <edge source="&quot;SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE&quot;" target="&quot;DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">1330.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde is responsible for the Departamento de Atenção Básica, which publishes Cadernos de Atenção Básica."&lt;SEP&gt;Here is a comprehensive summary of the data provided:

**Entities:** "DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA" (Department of Basic Attention) and "SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE" (Secretariat of Attention to Health)

The Department of Basic Attention (DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA) is a department within the Secretariat of Attention to Health (SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE), responsible for providing primary healthcare services. The Department operates under the Secretariat, indicating a clear administrative connection and hierarchical structure.

The Department works closely with the Secretariat on basic health care issues in Brazil, ensuring effective delivery of healthcare services and promoting preventive care. It provides primary healthcare services, including those related to smoking cessation, diabetes, and other chronic diseases.

The Secretariat oversees and guides the Department's work, ensuring effective delivery of healthcare services and promoting preventive care in Brazil. This close collaboration between the two entities enables them to share a common goal of delivering high-quality health services to various populations.

In addition, the Department reports directly to the Ministry of Health, which carries out its policies through the Department of Basic Attention. The Secretariat is responsible for overseeing the Department's work on basic healthcare services.

Therefore, the summary can be resolved as follows:

The **Department of Basic Attention** (DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA) is a department within the **Secretariat of Attention to Health** (SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE), responsible for providing primary healthcare services in Brazil. The Department operates under the Secretariat, and both entities work together to deliver high-quality health services to various populations.</data>
