    <edge source="&quot;SECRETARIA DE ATENÇÃO À SAÚDE&quot;" target="&quot;MINISTÉRIO DA SAÚDE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">1732.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Ministério da Saúde oversees the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde, which in turn manages the Departamento de Atenção Básica and publishes Cadernos de Atenção Básica."&lt;SEP&gt;Here is a comprehensive summary:

**The Ministério da Saúde (Ministry of Health) and the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde (Secretariat of Attention to Health)**

The Ministério da Saúde (Ministry of Health) and the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde (Secretariat of Attention to Health) are closely related entities that work together to address health issues in Brazil. The Ministry is the parent entity, and the Secretariat operates within it as a department responsible for healthcare attention.

**Relationship between Entities**

The Ministério da Saúde collaborates with the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde to develop health policies and guidelines, and it oversees the Secretariat's work on attention to health and disease prevention. The Secretary of Attention to Health reports to the Ministério da Saúde, indicating a hierarchical relationship.

**Structure**

The Ministério da Saúde has a department called Departamento de Atenção Básica (Department of Basic Attention) within it, which is responsible for basic care services under the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde. The Ministry appoints officials to the Secretariat for guidance on health policies, and the Secretary is responsible for developing policies and guidelines for healthcare in Brazil.

**Responsibilities**

The Ministério da Saúde is responsible for overall health policy in Brazil, while the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde implements basic care services, focusing on specific implementation and coordination. The Ministry oversees the Secretariat's work on health policies and strategies, ensuring continuity in healthcare services.

Together, the Ministério da Saúde and the Secretaria de Atenção à Saúde share a common goal of promoting healthy behaviors and addressing health issues in Brazil through effective policy-making, program implementation, and coordination.</data>
