    <edge source="&quot;DEPARTAMENTO DE ATENÇÃO BÁSICA&quot;" target="&quot;MINISTÉRIO DA SAÚDE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">983.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Here is a comprehensive summary of the provided data:

**Departamento de Atenção Básica (Basic Care Department) and Ministério da Saúde (Ministry of Health)**

The Departamento de Atenção Básica, also known as the Basic Care Department, operates under the guidance and direction of the Ministério da Saúde, the Ministry of Health. The Basic Care Department is responsible for providing primary care services to the public, implementing primary healthcare strategies, and working in tandem with national policies. It focuses on basic health care services and collaborates with the Ministry of Health to provide comprehensive health guidelines.

The Departamento de Atenção Básica belongs to the Ministry of Health, reports directly to it, and is responsible for basic healthcare services. The Ministério da Saúde oversees and guides the Departamento de Atenção Básica in its policies and operations, ensuring that guidelines and recommendations are followed by healthcare professionals.

Together, the Departamento de Atenção Básica and the Ministério da Saúde work to provide healthcare services and promote public health in Brazil. They collaborate on developing health guidelines and providing basic healthcare services, which falls under the Ministry of Health's jurisdiction.

There is no contradiction between the descriptions, and all information collected from them has been included in this comprehensive summary.</data>
