    <edge source="&quot;FASE INICIAL&quot;" target="&quot;SÍNDROME DO ENTARDECER&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The initial phase's symptoms progress to the twilight syndrome, characterized by confusion mental and behavioral alterations near sunset time."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cognitive decline, behavioral changes"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SÍNDROME DO ENTARDECER&quot;" target="&quot;FASE AVANÇADA OU ESTÁGIO TERMINAL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The twilight syndrome's symptoms worsen, leading to the advanced or terminal stage, where individuals are severely compromised cognitively and eventually become mute."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cognitive decline, progression to dementia"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FASE INTERMEDIÁRIA&quot;" target="&quot;FASE AVANÇADA OU ESTÁGIO TERMINAL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The intermediate phase's deterioration of cognitive functions leads to the advanced or terminal stage, marked by severe compromise of all cognitive abilities and eventual mutism."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cognitive decline, progression to dementia"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FASE INTERMEDIÁRIA&quot;" target="&quot;AFASIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Aphasia is a symptom of the intermediate phase, where individuals experience difficulty with language, including naming objects and understanding spoken words."</data>
      <data key="d5">"language impairment, cognitive decline"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FASE INTERMEDIÁRIA&quot;" target="&quot;AGNOSIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Agnosia is also a symptom of the intermediate phase, where individuals have difficulty recognizing objects, people, sounds, or shapes despite maintaining intact sensory function."</data>
      <data key="d5">"sensory impairment, cognitive decline"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FASE INTERMEDIÁRIA&quot;" target="&quot;APRAXIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Apraxia is another symptom of the intermediate phase, where individuals experience difficulty executing precise movements and gestures that require patterns of memory or sequential movement."</data>
      <data key="d5">"motor impairment, cognitive decline"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FASE AVANÇADA OU ESTÁGIO TERMINAL&quot;" target="&quot;SÍNDROME DA IMOBILIDADE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Syndrome of immobility leads to the advanced or terminal stage, where individuals are severely compromised cognitively and become bedridden."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cognitive decline, progression to dementia"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AVD&quot;" target="&quot;AIVD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"AIVD and AVD are stages of cognitive decline, with AIVD representing an earlier stage and AVD a later stage of deterioration."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cognitive decline, progression to dementia"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7c237c89e3d3730f160a6a8a3cf67ac7</data>
    </edge>
